<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Prile</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lacus Prilius</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Prile, the Roman Lacus Prilius, was a coastal lagoon in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruria">Etruria</a> near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grosseto">Grosseto</a>, fed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ombrone">Ombrone</a> and once open to the sea. The Etruscan cities of Vetulonia and Rusellae stood on hills above its shores and used it as a harbour. It gradually silted into marshland, the later Padule di Castiglione, and was drained between the 18th and 20th centuries.</p></div>
